<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">raise-golem</ansi> spell

The <ansi fg="command">Raise Golem</ansi> spell reshapes a corpse into a massive, lumbering
construct of flesh and bone that obliterates all in its path. Golems are
the ultimate expressions of necromantic power, brutal and unstoppable, and
they need the remains of truly magnificent creatures to sustain.

Golems are colossal melee combatants that crush foes with overwhelming
physical force. They move with the weight of small mountains, shaking the
earth beneath their feet.

The servant's power scales with your Charisma and manifestation skill, and
with the remains you raise it from. Part of it is drawn from the corpse, so
the same spell over better remains yields a better servant. A golem is the
most demanding of the raised undead to keep, and holding one will usually
mean holding little else.

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage: </ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">cast raise-golem [corpse]</ansi>     Animate nearby remains.

<ansi fg="yellow">Base Folds:  </ansi> Long channel
<ansi fg="yellow">Corpse:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Requires overwhelming remains</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Target:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Nearby corpse or ground loot</ansi>
<ansi fg="yellow">Cast Cost:   </ansi> Steep, and paid only once
<ansi fg="yellow">Held Cost:   </ansi> Heavy, for as long as you keep it
<ansi fg="yellow">School:      </ansi> <ansi fg="white-bold">Manifestation</ansi>

<ansi fg="white-bold">Notes:</ansi>
  - The golem appears under your command and aids you in combat.
  - Once raised, the undead servant remains active as a companion.
  - Use the <ansi fg="command">assess</ansi> command to evaluate a corpse's quality.
  - Raising costs conviction once. Keeping the servant sets conviction
    aside for as long as it walks with you, and that held share, not
    the casting price, is what limits how many you can field.
  - A mightier servant holds more of your will, and better remains
    make a mightier servant.
  - Skill in manifestation lowers what a companion holds, so practice
    buys you a larger following as well as a stronger one.
  - If your conviction is already spoken for, the raising is refused
    outright rather than leaving you weaker, and costs you nothing.

